⚙️ Installation
Clone the repository:
   git clone <your-repository-url>

Navigate to the project directory:
   cd log_analyzer

(Optional) Create and activate a virtual environment:
   python -m venv venv

Install dependencies if required:
   pip install -r requirements.txt

🚀 Usage

Run the Python script:

python log_analyzer.py


If your program accepts a log-file path as an argument, you can use:

python log_analyzer.py sample.log


The exact command depends on how your script is implemented.

🔎 Example Use Cases
Identifying repeated failed login attempts.
Detecting suspicious IP addresses.
Reviewing system errors and warnings.
Investigating unusual activity in application logs.
🔐 Security Note

This tool supports basic log analysis and does not replace a full Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) system. Detection accuracy depends on the log format and implemented rules.

